**Definition 8.3 (all successful entries and native handoffs).** The
following table, with Definition 2.3's inlining convention, specifies the
complete new successful finite control. No next publication starts with
the previous mailbox busy.

| Entry | Word/native work in order | Next actual entry |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Original ClientImage success | Position/import actual 73; original Image codec/binding checks. Construct $b$ from that acquired target. ACK Image, TOK mailbox availability back. Keep this flight's client invocation; do not append $M$ or enter Ready. TOK client→handler; CTL RenderS. | RenderS |
| RenderS | Parse the imported Image raw projection; component walker emits initial S candidate. Clear acquired Image work fields after construction; no later direct decoder reads them. | Publish0 |
| Publish0 | Export exact View stage 0, execute Definition 8.4, TOK handler→client, CTL CheckS0. | CheckS0 |
| CheckS0 | Position 73 from its current placement; clear candidate; actual F-bounded import into received, parse body to sourceBody, $D_S$/re-encode/binding checks; copy this received S to firstS. ACK/mailbox return, TOK client→handler, CTL FromS. | FromS |
| FromS | Clear derived work; Definition 7.3 FromS on sourceBody only; set candidate B. | Publish1 |
| Publish1 | Same publication with stage 1; actual handler→client TOK, CTL CheckB. | CheckB |
| CheckB | Position 73; clear candidate; import actual stage-1 B; $D_B$/re-encode/binding checks. ACK/mailbox return, TOK client→handler, CTL FromB. | FromB |
| FromB | Clear derived work; direct B→M on sourceBody; candidate is only M-body. | Publish2 |
| Publish2 | Same publication with stage 2; actual handler→client TOK, CTL CheckM. | CheckM |
| CheckM | Position 73; clear candidate; import actual M; $D_M$/reselect/binding checks. ACK/mailbox return, TOK client→handler, CTL FromM. | FromM |
| FromM | Clear derived work; direct M→T; candidate is only occurrence list. | Publish3 |
| Publish3 | Same publication with stage 3; actual handler→client TOK, CTL CheckT. | CheckT |
| CheckT | Position 73; clear candidate; import actual T; $D_T$/record/binding checks. ACK/mailbox return, TOK client→handler, CTL FromT. | FromT |
| FromT | Clear derived work; direct T→S; candidate is only final mask word. | Publish4 |
| Publish4 | Same publication with stage 4; actual handler→client TOK, CTL CheckS1. | CheckS1 |
| CheckS1 | Position 73; clear candidate; import final S; run $D_S$/re-encode/binding checks; Equal its received body with firstS. Serialize its independently decoded historical prefix/raw record as the legacy Image value and apply original ClientImage's Image checker subgraph. | FinalReturn |
| FinalReturn | ACK this channel once; TOK mailbox availability back; append one completed history-cycle item with original supplied frame and typed outcome/bindings; TOK invocation to outer client; CTL Ready. | Actual $R_r$ |

All callback checks use a body actually read from 73. Neither the initial
Image nor firstS repairs a decoder: firstS is read only by the final Equal
comparison. The original checker at CheckS1 consumes the decoded value,
not the initial Image. There is no repair branch. No external input or
optional scheduling step occurs between these entries.

The reused `CheckImageValue` is exactly ClientImage's finite word parser
and source/version/$p,c,k,\varrho$ comparison subgraph, factored after its
receiver import and before its ACK. It is inlined with a word argument.
At CheckS1 construct the exact legacy Image wrapper
`[0010,serviceBinding,xi,U(p),U(c),U(k),rho,image]` from the newly decoded
prefix/raw record and apply that subgraph. It performs no second receiver
import or synthetic channel handoff. The one ACK is FinalReturn's actual
ACK for the received S publication. Initial Image success still performs
its own actual import/check/ACK before RenderS.

